# Sample requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (click "Send Request").
# Bruno and Postman can import or copy these too.
@base = http://localhost:3000
# Send "Log in as admin" first: the write requests below reuse its token.
@admin = Bearer {{adminLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Health
GET {{base}}/health

### API docs: open {{base}}/docs in a browser. The raw OpenAPI document:
GET {{base}}/openapi.json

### --- Auth ---

### Sign up (always creates a regular user)
POST {{base}}/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "ana@example.com", "password": "correct-horse", "name": "Ana" }

### Log in as admin
# @name adminLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "admin@example.com", "password": "admin-password" }

### Log in as the demo user
# @name userLogin
POST {{base}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "user@example.com", "password": "user-password" }

### Who am I?
GET {{base}}/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Exchange the refresh token for a new pair (works once per token)
POST {{base}}/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{userLogin.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### Log out (revokes the refresh token)
POST {{base}}/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{ "refreshToken": "{{userLogin.response.body.refreshToken}}" }

### Promote user 2 to admin (admin only)
PATCH {{base}}/users/2/role
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "admin" }

### 403: a regular user trying to create a movie
POST {{base}}/movies
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Nope", "description": "Not allowed", "durationMinutes": 90 }

### --- Genres ---

### List genres
GET {{base}}/genres

### Create a genre
POST {{base}}/genres
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Thriller" }

### --- Movies ---

### List movies (paginated, optional ?genre=<id>)
GET {{base}}/movies?page=1&limit=20

### Movies in one genre
GET {{base}}/movies?genre=3

### Get one movie
GET {{base}}/movies/1

### Create a movie
POST {{base}}/movies
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Arrival",
  "description": "A linguist is recruited to talk with alien visitors.",
  "posterUrl": "https://example.com/posters/arrival.jpg",
  "durationMinutes": 116,
  "genreIds": [3, 4]
}

### Update some fields (genreIds replaces the whole list)
PATCH {{base}}/movies/4
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "Arrival (2016)", "genreIds": [4] }

### Delete a movie (409 if it has showtimes, like movie 1)
DELETE {{base}}/movies/4
Authorization: {{admin}}

### --- Browsing (public) ---
# The seed schedules showtimes for tomorrow and the 2 days after (UTC). Change the date.

### Movies with their upcoming showtimes on a day (theater timezone, default UTC)
GET {{base}}/movies/showtimes?date=2026-10-19

### Same day, as seen from Tokyo (UTC+9): a different set of showtimes
GET {{base}}/movies/showtimes?date=2026-10-19&tz=Asia/Tokyo

### Seat map of a showtime (seats A1 and A2 are taken in the seed)
GET {{base}}/showtimes/1/seats

### --- Reservations (logged-in users) ---
# Send "Log in as the demo user" first. Seat ids: Hall 1 is 1-40 (A1=1 ... E8=40), Hall 2 is 41-64.

### Book seats B1 and B2 for showtime 1 (the server computes the total)
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "showtimeId": 1, "seatIds": [9, 10] }

### 409 SEATS_TAKEN: A1 is booked in the seed
POST {{base}}/reservations
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "showtimeId": 1, "seatIds": [1] }

### My reservations (newest showtime first, paginated)
GET {{base}}/reservations/me
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### One reservation (yours, or any if you're an admin)
GET {{base}}/reservations/1
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### Cancel (only yours, only upcoming); the seats become free again
POST {{base}}/reservations/1/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{userLogin.response.body.accessToken}}

### --- Showtimes ---
# Times must include a timezone: "Z" (UTC) or an offset like "-06:00".
# The seed schedules showtimes for the next 3 days; pick a date after them.

### Get one showtime (public)
GET {{base}}/showtimes/1

### Create a showtime (ends_at = start + duration + cleaning buffer)
POST {{base}}/showtimes
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "movieId": 3, "hallId": 2, "startsAt": "2030-01-15T20:00:00Z", "priceCents": 1100 }

### 409 HALL_BUSY: same hall, overlapping time (send the one above first)
POST {{base}}/showtimes
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "movieId": 1, "hallId": 2, "startsAt": "2030-01-15T21:00:00Z", "priceCents": 1100 }

### Same time in another hall is fine
POST {{base}}/showtimes
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "movieId": 1, "hallId": 1, "startsAt": "2030-01-15T21:00:00Z", "priceCents": 1100 }

### Change only the price (always allowed before it starts)
PATCH {{base}}/showtimes/1
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "priceCents": 1300 }

### 409: showtime 1 has a reservation, so it can't move
PATCH {{base}}/showtimes/1
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "startsAt": "2030-01-16T18:00:00Z" }

### 409: can't delete a showtime that has reservations
DELETE {{base}}/showtimes/1
Authorization: {{admin}}

### --- Admin reports (send "Log in as admin" first) ---
# from/to filter on when the SHOW starts: from inclusive, to exclusive, with a timezone.

### Every reservation, filtered and paginated
GET {{base}}/admin/reservations?status=confirmed&page=1&limit=20
Authorization: {{admin}}

### Per showtime: capacity, tickets sold, occupancy, revenue (cancelled seats don't count)
GET {{base}}/admin/reports/showtimes?from=2026-10-19T00:00:00Z&to=2026-10-20T00:00:00Z
Authorization: {{admin}}

### Per movie: revenue and tickets (movies with no showtimes in the range show zeros)
GET {{base}}/admin/reports/movies
Authorization: {{admin}}

### --- Errors to try ---

### 400: several validation problems at once
POST {{base}}/movies
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title": "", "durationMinutes": -5, "posterUrl": "javascript:alert(1)" }

### 400: malformed JSON
POST {{base}}/movies
Authorization: {{admin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "title":
